```text
RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE

Office of City Clerk

March 5, 2020

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date
beginning at 6:00p.m. in City Council Chambers for the purpose of collective labor bargaining
with the Cheyenne Professional Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local
No. 279.  Present were:  MAYOR - Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS – Bryan Cook, Ken
Esquibel, Pete Laybourn, Mike Luna, Dicky Shanor, and Jeff White.  Absent:  Rocky Case and
Dr. Mark Rinne and Scott Roybal.  Also present: Kris Jones, City Clerk; Michael O’Donnell, City
Attorney; Alessandra McCoy-Fakelman, Deputy City Attorney, Robin Lockman, City Treasurer,
and Chief Greg Hoggatt, Fire and Rescue Department.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Mayor Orr requested those who may be speaking to use the microphones so that their
comments can be heard.  Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded and available
on Facebook live and stated that Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings
Act allows the governing body to meet in executive session to consider or tender offers regarding
salaries, wages or other terms and conditions of employment during negotiations with the fire
fighters union and that any motion approved by the governing body to move into executive session
during the special meetings would be pursuant to this section of statute.  Mayor Orr further advised
if the governing body met in executive session, they would be meeting in the Mayor’s Conference
Room, and that Fire Union representatives were welcome to use Committee Room 104 for the
purpose of meeting to caucus.

 Michael O’Donnell, City Attorney, advised the City would be presenting a counteroffer
following an executive session by the Governing Body.

 Pursuant to Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x), Mr. Luna moved to meet in executive
session, seconded by Mr. White.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing
body present.  Mayor Orr identified, in addition to members of the governing body present, the
City Clerk, City Attorney, Deputy City Attorney, City Treasurer, and Chief of the Fire and Rescue
Department would also be present at the executive session.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of
the special meeting was stopped; executive session convened at 6:07 p.m. in the Mayor’s
Conference Room]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at
7:03 p.m.

 Kevin West, Union Representative, advised Sections #12-Union Representation and #34-
Union Dues, have been closed and require signatures by both parties.

Michael O’Donnell, City Attorney, presented the Union representatives with the City’s
counteroffer and provided a brief summary on each section.  The following Sections contained a
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
revised offer from the City: 3-Exclusive Bargaining Agent, 8-Grievance Procedures, 18-Trading
Shifts, 22-Overtime, 25-Conversion of Benefit Hours, 33-Personal Protective Equipment-City
accepts Union offer, and 37-Time Off for Union Business.  Mr. O’Donnell advised the remaining
open sections are re-offered as originally offered by the City:  Sections 2-Definitions, 13-
Management Rights, 15-Department Staffing, 17-Hours of Work, 19-Inclement Weather
Conditions, 20-Holidays, 23-Working in a Higher Job Rank, 24-Specialized Emergency Response
Teams, 26-Wellness/Fitness Program, 28-Sick Leave and 41-Prevailing Rights.

Mayor Orr clarified that although the City supports the concept of forming a “Squad” with
personnel for the Fire Department, the City is not including it in the contract at this time.   Upon
inquiry from Mr. O’Donnell, Mr. West confirmed Sections 46-Military Leave, 47-Tuition
Reimbursement and 48-Parental Leave were previously closed.

Pursuant to Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x), Mr. Luna moved to meet in executive
session, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing
body present.  Mayor Orr identified, in addition to members of the governing body present, the
City Clerk, City Attorney, Deputy City Attorney, City Treasurer, and Chief of the Fire and Rescue
Department would also be present at the executive session.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of
the special meeting was stopped; executive Session convened at 7:18 p.m. in the Mayor’s
Conference Room] [Additional Clerk note:  The purpose of the executive session was to allow
Union representatives the opportunity to caucus to review the City’s offer]

Mr. Laybourn excused himself for the remainder of the meeting due to a previous
commitment during executive session at 7:45 p.m.

Following a request from Union representatives at 7:51 p.m., Mr. White moved to extend
the time for the executive session, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body present.

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at
8:19 p.m.

Mr. West provided a brief explanation of the Union’s counteroffer with changes to the
following Sections:  13-Management Rights, 15-Department Staffing, 20-Holidays, 21-
Classification of Employment and Basic Wages, 22-Overtime, 23-Working in a Higher Job Rank,
24-Specialized Emergency Response Teams, 25-Conversion of Benefit Hours, (23, 24, and 25-
Union accepts City’s offer) 26-Wellness/Fitness Program, 37-Time off for Union Business and
41-Prevailing Rights.  Mr. West advised remaining open sections are re-offered as originally
offered.

Mr. O’Donnell, upon inquiry from Mr. West, advised closed sections will be signed off at
the beginning of the next scheduled meeting on March 10, 2020 beginning at 6:00 PM in Council
Chambers, 2101 O’Neil Ave.
```

